notes.content:
[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
- Fixed the bug when save file names are invalid, the game couldn't be started;
- Fixed the display bug of card re-lock status after Big Bangs;
- Fixed the bug with equipping/unequipping the card Mysterious Meat;
- Fixed Max Damage Dealt in Stats;
- Fixed Chinese and Japanese font issues;
- Fixed the travel progress requirement of the Achievement 'That Speedy Planet';
- Fixed a bug that prevented Mac players from loading the game;
- Fixed offline progress simulation;
- Optimised memory usage, but we are still working on further optimisations;

[b]Feature Updates:[/b]
- Dark Matter calculation formula is now visible in the Big Bang page;
- Added Stardust amount labels to the Card Forging and Card Alchemy tabs;
- Some Epic (golden) perm cards are passively effective (no need to equip them)! We added an explanation in their tooltips;

[b]Content Updates:[/b]
- Made Dark Matter calculation more powerful;
- Improved the Big Bang Upgrade 'Biologically Advanced Universe';
- Added new Big Bang upgrades boosting Card Alchemy probabilities and Stardust Gain (we will show Card Alchemy probabilities in the next patch);
- Adjusted prices of Big Bang Upgrades (Because of this, your Dark Matter amount might appear as negative number.);
- Removed the Metal requirement to travel to the Sun, and changed the building requirements for Rocket Launcher Pad on the Sun;
- Added a new production on the Spaceship which produces Biomass, and a research to unlock it;
- Slightly adjusted early-game contents (Earth and Moon);
- Added a few new cards in the enemy drops in zone Acid Clouds, Martian Highlands, Martian Invasion and Martian Dungeons;
- Pekky's Panties now drops from Volcanic Eruption's boss;
- Added a new Alchemy Card;

Version 0.3.5.33

[b]Feature Updates:[/b]
- Added a toggle in settings to hide/show card setting UIs;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
- Fixed Card setting slider UI related bugs;
- Fixed a bug that menus are locked when traveling. Now they should be visible again;

Version 0.3.5.32

[b]Content:[/b]
- New location content：Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, Pluto;

[b]Feature Updates:[/b]
- Added Big Bang Feature (Prestige System);
- Added Tutorials;
- Added Missions - Achievements;
- Added Stats menu;
- Added offline progress logging;

[b]Updated Discord Server Invitation Link:[/b]
discord.gg/WrwuNqaees

Bug fixes:
- Fixed a bug when reaching new location while offline, new content not being displayed error;
- Fixed Library card level slider bugs;

Version 0.2.2.5

Feature Updates:
- Show level indicator on card level slider handle when dragging;
- Show merge progress to the next level card in card stacks;

Bug fixes:
- Fixed a bug that newly added card levels aren't shown in the card stack;
- Fixed a display bug in max Biomass/sec in Asteroid Belt information;
- Fixed save file list loading bug;
- Fixed a bug that when loading saves progress stucks at the beginning;
- Fixed the error that recent new players see no researches, infras and cards when loading save;
- Fixed card stack slider dragging error;

Version 0.2.2.3

Feature Updates:
- Now in card settings, by default 0 card is protected instead of 1;
- Added all level protect count and apply buttons in card settings;

This update is mainly for the Card Bag UI upgrade.
In addition, we've also done the save data migration to make sure no more save data wipes in the future.

The next regular update will likely be the [b]Card Alchemy[/b], where you can combine different cards to create new cards! Make sure to keep some max-level cards in your bag in preparation for it.

[b]Patch Notes:[/b]
Version 0.2.2.2

Feature Updates:
- Cards are now displayed in stacks;
- Implemented Card Settings! Configure auto sell and protection count in the settings;
- Library unknown card names now show as "????";
- Only collectible cards are displayed in the Library now;

Content Updates:
- Enhanced iron and energy production on Venus;
- Enhanced Space Folding I slightly;
- Increased max levels of Higher Quality Steel and Heat Resistant Equipments (Total bonus unchanged);
- Increased max level and max bonus of Path Knowledge I;
- Lowered Mercury's recommended departure stats;
- Added 2 new battle cards;
- Preparation for Sun and Mars content;

Performance:
- Greatly reduced save file size;

Content Updates:
- Access to 2 new locations: Mercury and Sun;
- Added nearly 30 new cards;
- Added a few more Battle Zones;

Feature Updates:
- Offline progress for Battle is available now! After unlocking this feature, you will gain Stardust when you are offline;
- Card Forging using Stardust;
- The AI scripting tool that will allow those players interested in programming to practice optimizing their battle AI in a playful manner;
- A new language: German;
- An overhaul and modernization of resources and their collection methods;
- Perhaps most importantly, a comprehensive help-book that will serve as an in-game tutorial (for now);
- Lots of other new stuff!

Bug Fixes:
- Many more fixes to the pre-release version!

Build 0.1.5.7:

Bug fixes:
    - Fixed biomass drop amount display bug (the amount you actually get was correct);
    - Infra Restructure card's Energy Gain effect is working now;
    - Fixed Japanese text wrapping bug

Build 0.1.5.6

Bug fixes:
    - Fixed a bug of internal numbers loaded incorrectly across different countries;
    - Fixed a bug that cards can be upgraded beyond the level limits;

Build 0.1.5.2b

Bug fixes:
    - When arriving at a new star, its Infra/Research list will be shown;
    - Fixed a bug that water and soil are unable to be discarded;
    - Fixed a bug of logging '0 damage' when an attack is actually 'missed'. Now it will log 'miss';
    - Productions will stop when the output energy/element is full;
    - Fixed a bug that can set off for the star you are staying (for real) :P

Feature Updates:
    - Enlarged the star selector at Techno Panel;
    - Changed to an English font which is not that annoying;
    - Numbers will be shown in 2 decimal places instead of 4;
    - Show max input/output per second instead of per tick;
    - Moved Infra energy cost per second out of tooltip to show it more clearly;

Content Updates:
    - Added a very expensive coal source on the moon

Build 0.1.5.1b

Bug fixes:
    - Fixed Battle Log card level display bug;
    - Storage panel's drag controls now won't loop when reached the first or last item;
    - Fix a display bug in Card Set tooltip;
    - Changed wordings of Card Set tooltips;
    - Fix a bug that Crater Guard boss not showing up;
    - Typo fixes;
    - Fixed some auto battle behaviours of enemies;
    - Fix a bug that some infras running at excessive speed;
    - Fix a bug that can set off for the star you are staying :P

Feature Updates:
    - Some drag controls now supports vertical dragging;
    - Added Research Target Level;
    - Added Infra Target Level and Turn On Level;
    - Display Energy/Resource max amount and percentage;
    - Reordered some menu buttons;
    - Now deteriorated efficiency will be calculated in Energy/Element outputs;
    - Elaborated the tooltip for Speed Module on instructions of filtering Energy;
    - Now fullscreen/window mode can be toggled in System Panel, and window will be resizable;
    - Added Exit button in System Panel;
